  "notes": "{寄与|きよ} combines {寄|き} (to approach, to contribute) and {与|よ} (to give). It is a formal word used in written and official contexts.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {社会|しゃかい}に{寄与|きよ}する (to contribute to society)\n- {発展|はってん}に{寄与|きよ}する (to contribute to development)\n- {寄与|きよ}{度|ど} (degree of contribution)\n- {寄与|きよ}が{大|おお}きい (significant contribution)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {寄与|きよ} vs. {貢献|こうけん}: Both mean \"contribution,\" but {寄与|きよ} is more formal and literary. {貢献|こうけん} is the more common, everyday word. {寄与|きよ} often appears in academic, legal, and official writing.",
